  "F|Same-scene presence and costume lock — 同场在场人物入画 + 服装锁": "F-001",
  "F|第2、3集通过后转正：**Face-state lock follows the story (TR-V01).** A visible story state on the face (tiredness, puffy eyelids, eye bags, a fresh look after a win) has a start beat and an end beat from the novel. Before the end beat every shot of that character writes the state; from the end beat on every shot writes the new state and binds the matching state image if an approved one exists. Never write the state in only some shots. Write the state by shape and degree only, never by colour or darkness words around the eyes (manual M50 item 2). Wrong: the tired face written in #3 and #9 only. Right: `<name>'s lower eyelids are puffy and swollen, with clear eye bags.` in every shot before the beat; `<name>'s face is fresh and rested; the lower eyelids are smooth.` in every shot after it.": "F-002",
  "F|第2、3集通过后转正：**Prop size lock (TR-V03).** A prop whose reference is a multi-view or a sized sheet gets one fixed real-world size sentence in every shot it appears in: `The <prop> is <real-world size copied from the prop asset sheet> and it never grows or shrinks.`": "F-003",
  "F|第2、3集通过后转正：**Adjacent-shot position lock (TR-V10).** Every shot of a scene states who is on which side of whom (also after a push, pull or hug). Only for two shots in the same scene where the action is continuous does the next shot open with `The characters keep the same left-right positions as in the previous shot.` followed by who is on which side. After a camera change, a jump cut or a time skip, write only who is on which side of whom in the new framing. Describe people's positions only; never write a sentence that locks the camera or the frame to the previous shot. Right (continuous push): #12 opens `The characters keep the same left-right positions as in the previous shot: Han Zixiao stays on screen-left of Jiang Che.` Right (#13 cuts to the reverse angle): `Han Zixiao is on Jiang Che's right, between him and the door.` Wrong: opening #13 with a sentence that ties its camera to the last frame of #12.": "F-004",
  "F|第2、3集通过后转正：**Every shot binds a scene (TR-V12).** `scene_ids` is never empty; the gate already stops an empty `scene_ids` as an error (SCENE_UNBOUND). Same-scene shots share one scene sentence (see item 14 \"Scene lock\" in the section \"Same-scene presence and costume lock — 同场在场人物入画 + 服装锁\" above).": "F-005",
  "F|**Hand props: write where the prop stays and where it never goes.** When a character holds anything that could go to the face (cup, glass, bottle, can, phone, cigarette, food, chopsticks), write its position for the whole shot, e.g. `she holds the cup at chest level the whole time; it never goes to her mouth`. If the story needs a sip or a call, write the exact second it is raised and when it comes down, and keep the mouth clear during any `<d>` line (see the dialogue-window section).": "F-006",
  "F|**No glasses unless the story gives a reason.** Write `no glasses` into each character's lock (the look / costume lock sentence). A character who wears glasses by design keeps the same pair in every shot (`wears the thin black-rimmed glasses from his reference`); glasses never appear, disappear or change mid-shot.": "F-007",
