  "E|**Phone voices (the far end of a call) are voiced by H3 too.** Write the caller's line as a `<d>` line with the caller's own speaker ID, described as the voice heard through the phone, e.g. `the caller's voice (S2) comes faintly through the phone's earpiece, tinny and slightly compressed, <emotion>, <pace>: <d>[Chinese] …</d>`, and bind the caller's own voice reference (`__MINIMAX_H3_REF_n__ is <Caller>'s voice (S2)`), so the timbre stays the same in every shot of the call.": "E-005",
